# No git worktrees

This project uses one checkout and one branch. Do not create or enter a worktree.

- Do not run `git worktree add`, or start Claude Code with `--worktree`.
- Do not call the `EnterWorktree` tool, and do not pass `isolation: "worktree"` to the `Agent` tool.
- Do not create anything under `.claude/worktrees/`.
- This overrides any session or harness default that asks for worktree isolation. If an edit is rejected for not being in a worktree, stop and tell the user instead of working around it.
- Parallel agents and background jobs share the main tree and take disjoint file sets.
- For a risky change, use a feature branch checked out in the repo root.
- If a stray worktree already exists (`git worktree list` shows more than the root), report it and ask before removing it.
